Add sync header dependency for entrypoint library on all platforms (fixes iOS build, QTBUG-151960)

https://qt-project.atlassian.net/browse/QTBUG-151960
https://github.com/qt/qtbase/commit/55d3591740


From 55d3591740d60f4c3e1c75782c9770c81801ff55 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Viktor Arvidsson
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 13:11:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Add sync header dependency for entrypoint library on all
 platforms
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The EntryPointImplementation library picks up QtCore's include
directories via a generator expression, which doesn't add a target
dependency on Core_sync_headers. We only added that dependency
explicitly for Windows, as the library was Windows-only at the time.

In 4fc36aa558b7b79bdf1171cd49c22398e885b1dd we started building
qtentrypoint_ios.mm as part of the library, but without the
dependency, so builds that don't sync headers at configure time
could compile it before the QtCore headers were generated.

    fatal error: 'QtCore/qprocessordetection.h' file not found

Developer builds and static Ninja Multi-Config builds both sync at
configure time, which is why neither local builds nor CI caught it.

Amends 4fc36aa558b7b79bdf1171cd49c22398e885b1dd.

Fixes: QTBUG-151960
Change-Id: I22f0f0c301b39f05abcacf40461944024ca0ebac
Reviewed-by: Tor Arne Vestbø <tor.arne.vestbo@qt.io>
(cherry picked from commit d5dcc7f776938d6156781a18fa973de70daf2bd1)
Reviewed-by: Qt Cherry-pick Bot <cherrypick_bot@qt-project.org>
---
 src/entrypoint/CMakeLists.txt | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/entrypoint/CMakeLists.txt b/src/entrypoint/CMakeLists.txt
index 79da1500cf5..77c3a00ea1a 100644
--- a/src/entrypoint/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/entrypoint/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -82,6 +82,7 @@ if(using_entrypoint_library)
     qt_handle_multi_config_output_dirs(EntryPointImplementation)
     qt_internal_add_target_aliases(EntryPointImplementation)
     qt_set_common_target_properties(EntryPointImplementation)
+    qt_internal_add_sync_header_dependencies(EntryPointImplementation Core)
 endif()
 
 # ---- Now we're ready to set up the platform specifics ----
@@ -109,8 +110,6 @@ if(WIN32)
         target_compile_definitions(EntryPointPrivate INTERFACE QT_NEEDS_QMAIN)
         qt_internal_extend_target(EntryPointImplementation DEFINES QT_NEEDS_QMAIN)
     endif()
-
-    qt_internal_add_sync_header_dependencies(EntryPointImplementation Core)
 endif()
 
 if(UIKIT)
